Build kefir's wasm32-wasip1 checker for fuzzing (--cfg fuzzing only)

kefir already builds for wasm32-wasip1 (the arena's kefir-wasm entry), with
a 256 MiB linear-memory stack, a 2 GiB initial memory and MAX_DEPTH
400 000, sized for Node running it on a 2 GiB engine stack. Under
--cfg fuzzing (build.rs sees CARGO_CFG_FUZZING):
- the module links with the suite's 16 MiB stack (FUZZING_STACK_BYTES,
  also the CHECK_STACK the stack guard measures against) and no
  --initial-memory, since fuzzers cap linear memory far below 2 GiB;
- STACK_BUDGET keeps a quarter of the stack (at most 64 MiB, as before)
  for the frames between checks, so it does not underflow on 16 MiB;
- MAX_DEPTH is 4096: wasm guest calls run on the engine's native stack,
  which wasmfuzz keeps at 8 MiB (run-input) to 32 MiB (fuzzing workers).
Builds without the cfg are unchanged.
Upstream: none (issues disabled upstream, no PRs, checked 2026-11-22).

